ntecedent of this rule is false, so the conclusion (bear chases the bald eagle) is not triggered.\n\n3. **Analysis**:.\n   - The bear’s actions are explicitly limited to chasing the lion and visiting the bald eagle and squirrel. No rule or fact forces the bear to chase the bald eagle.\n   - While the bald eagle is inferred to chase the bear (due to Rule 2), this does not affect the bear’s potential actions toward the bald eagle.\n   - No contradiction exists that would make the bear chasing the bald eagle impossible. However, there is no evidence supporting it either.\n\n**Conclusion**: The statement is neither explicitly supported nor contradicted by the given information. Therefore, it is **unknown**. Therefore, my final option is: ']]  0%|          | 2/600 [00:28<2:12:20, 13.28s/it]
