.\n\n3. **Lion's Age**:\n   - The lion visits the cat (statement 9).\n   - By statement 19 (\"If something visits the cat and it is not nice then it is young\"), since the lion visits the cat and is not nice, the lion must be young.\n\n4. **Verification**:\n   - If the lion were not young, there would be a contradiction with statement 19 because the antecedent (visits the cat and not nice) would be true, but the consequent (young) would be false.\n   - Therefore, the lion must be young.\n\nSince the lion is young, the statement \"The lion is not young\" is false. The correct answer is **B) False**.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
