ing kind). His color is otherwise unspecified.\n   - **Quietness**:\n     - There is no rule that directly links being non-kind to being quiet or not quiet.\n     - Quietness is not restricted to kind/nice people (e.g., Anne is quiet but not nice).\n     - Bob could be either quiet or not quiet without violating any rules.\n\n### Conclusion:\nSince there is no rule that definitively determines Bob's quietness, both possibilities (quiet or not quiet) are logically consistent. Therefore, the statement \"Bob is not quiet\" is **unknown**.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
