      "text": " B) False.\n</think>\n\nB) False\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Dave's Attributes:**\n   - Given: Dave is cold (fact 3) and furry (fact 4).\n   - From the conditional statement (11): If Dave is furry and cold \u2192 Dave is young. Since both conditions are true, **Dave is young**.\n   - From statement (15): If someone is young \u2192 they are kind. Thus, **Dave is kind**.\n\n2. **Determining if Dave is Nice:**\n   - From statement (16): All kind, cold people are nice. Dave is both kind (from step 1) and cold (given). Therefore, **Dave must be nice**.\n\n3. **Additional Consistency Checks:**\n   - By statement (12): All nice, cold people are red. Since Dave is nice and cold, he must be red.\n   - By statement (13): Red, young people are blue. Dave is red (from above) and young (from step 1), so he must also be blue. This is consistent with Fiona\u2019s attributes (blue and red) and no contradictions arise.\n\n**Conclusion:** The statement \"Dave is not nice\" is **false** because Dave is logically determined to be nice. \n\n**Answer:** B) False",
      "logprobs": null,
